      {
        "id": "p9-q2-k",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "k",
        "prompt": "$\\frac{1}{x-1}-\\frac{1}{x+3}=\\frac{1}{35}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=-13$ or $x=11$.\n\nMultiply by $35(x-1)(x+3)$, then factorise.",
          "worked": "Here $x\\ne1,-3$. Multiply by $35(x-1)(x+3)$.\n$$\\begin{align*}35(x+3)-35(x-1)&=(x-1)(x+3)\\\\140&=x^2+2x-3\\\\x^2+2x-143&=0\\\\(x+13)(x-11)&=0\\\\x&=-13\\text{ or }x=11\\end{align*}$$\nBoth values are permitted.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 62
      },
      {
        "id": "p9-q2-l",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "l",
        "prompt": "$\\frac{4}{x-1}-\\frac{5}{x+2}=\\frac{3}{x}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=-\\frac12$ or $x=3$.\n\nClear the denominators, then factorise the resulting quadratic.",
          "worked": "Here $x\\ne1,-2,0$. Multiply by $x(x-1)(x+2)$.\n$$\\begin{align*}4x(x+2)-5x(x-1)&=3(x-1)(x+2)\\\\4x^2+8x-5x^2+5x&=3x^2+3x-6\\\\-x^2+13x&=3x^2+3x-6\\\\4x^2-10x-6&=0\\\\2x^2-5x-3&=0\\\\(2x+1)(x-3)&=0\\\\x&=-\\frac12\\text{ or }x=3\\end{align*}$$\nBoth values are permitted.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 78
      },
      {
        "id": "p9-q2-m",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "m",
        "prompt": "$6(4x+5)+\\frac{7}{x}(4x+5)=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=-\\frac54$ or $x=-\\frac76$.",
          "worked": "For $x\\ne0$, multiply by $x$ and factorise.\n$$\\begin{align*}6x(4x+5)+7(4x+5)&=0\\\\(4x+5)(6x+7)&=0\\\\4x+5&=0\\text{ or }6x+7=0\\\\x&=-\\frac54\\text{ or }x=-\\frac76\\end{align*}$$\nBoth values are permitted.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 48
      },
      {
        "id": "p9-q2-n",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "n",
        "prompt": "$\\frac{2}{x+3}+\\frac{x+3}{2}=\\frac{10}{3}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=-\\frac73$ or $x=3$.\n\nMultiply by $6(x+3)$, expand and factorise.",
          "worked": "For $x\\ne-3$, multiply by $6(x+3)$.\n$$\\begin{align*}12+3(x+3)^2&=20(x+3)\\\\12+3x^2+18x+27&=20x+60\\\\3x^2-2x-21&=0\\\\(3x+7)(x-3)&=0\\\\x&=-\\frac73\\text{ or }x=3\\end{align*}$$\nBoth values are permitted.",
